// Distribution configuration (project level): an optimized build like Release, signed with a
// real identity and running with the hardened runtime, as notarized distribution outside the
// App Store requires. Debug and Release stay ad hoc signed without the hardened runtime, so they
// build and launch headless with no developer account.
//
// Why a separate configuration: the hardened runtime turns on library validation, which only
// loads embedded code signed by Apple or with the same Team ID as the app. Ad hoc signatures
// have no Team ID, so an ad hoc build with the hardened runtime aborts at launch (dyld cannot
// load VidEditEngine.framework or the FFmpeg dylibs). With a real identity every embedded
// library is re-signed with the app's identity when it is copied (CodeSignOnCopy), so they share
// its Team ID and load.
//
// Set the identity and team without editing tracked files, either
//   - in Config/Signing.local.xcconfig (gitignored), for example:
//         VIDEDIT_CODE_SIGN_IDENTITY = Developer ID Application
//         VIDEDIT_DEVELOPMENT_TEAM = ABCDE12345
//   - or on the xcodebuild command line: VIDEDIT_DEVELOPMENT_TEAM=ABCDE12345
// project.yml maps them onto CODE_SIGN_IDENTITY and DEVELOPMENT_TEAM for Distribution. Without
// a team the build stops with Xcode's "requires selecting a development team" error.

VIDEDIT_CODE_SIGN_IDENTITY = Developer ID Application
VIDEDIT_DEVELOPMENT_TEAM =

#include? "Signing.local.xcconfig"
